🕒 Overview

This project is a clock and time‑management application written in Python.
It allows the user to:

    display the system time in real time
    set a custom time that increments like a real clock
    switch between 24‑hour and 12‑hour AM/PM format
    configure an alarm
    use an interactive menu

📂 Project Structure

project/
│
├── main.py
├── alarm.py
├── printTime.py
└── changeformat.py

▶️ How to Run

Run the program with:

python main.py

Make sure the file alarm.mp3 is in the same folder for the alarm sound.
📌 Features
1) Main Menu (main.py)

Displayed menu:

===== MENU =====
1. Show Clock
2. Set time
3. Alarm
4. Stop time
5. AM / PM
6. Quit

Only options 1, 2, 3, and 5 are functional.
2) 🕰 Show System Time (printTime.py)

Function: print_time()

    Displays the system time live
    Updates every second
    Uses \r to refresh on the same line
    Stop by pressing A

Example:

Current time: 14:32:05

3) ⏱ Manual Time (printTime.py)
imput_time()

    Prompts the user to enter a valid hour, minute, and second (0–23 / 0–59 / 0–59)

set_time()

    Starts a custom clock from the chosen time
    Correct increments of hours, minutes, and seconds
    Stop by pressing A

Example:

Elapsed time: 08:12:53

4) ⏰ Alarm System (alarm.py)
alarm()

    Asks for hour and minute
    Validates input
    Starts a daemon thread to monitor the time
    Prints: Alarm activated…

show_alarm()

    Checks the current time every second
    When the set time matches, displays:

IT'S TIME !
ALARM - Is : 07 : 30
======================

    Plays alarm.mp3 in a separate thread

5) 🌓 AM / PM Format (changeformat.py)

Function: change_format()

    Displays time in either 24‑hour or 12‑hour format
    Press 1 to switch mode
    Press ESC to exit

Example:

14:08:12 To change mode press '1', 'esc' to exit
2:08:12 PM : To change mode press '1', 'esc' to exit

🛠 Requirements

Install required modules:

pip install playsound
pip install keyboard

📄 Notes

    The program uses threads so the alarm does not block the menu.
    The keyboard module may require administrator privileges on Windows.
    The file alarm.mp3 must be present in the project folder.
